{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999669-freebie-points-and-willpower","id":999669,"title":"Freebie points and Willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T04:59:13-08:00","id":999669,"title":"Freebie points and Willpower","content":"One thing that have always get me into trouble is the low freebie cost for increasing Willpower.<br /> <br /> I mean, Willpower is one of the most powerfull trait in each of the classic world of darkness games. Only one freebie for one dot is too easy in my opinion. I can\u2019t find a good reason of creating a character without using freebie in order to raise Willpower at 10.<br /> <br /> Okay GM can rule otherwise, or you can restrain yourself, but would it not be better to align Willpower cost with freebie as for xp?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm interested to read your opinion on that subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3879-black-lion","name":"Black Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:32:27-08:00","id":999677,"title":"","content":"I completely agree, based on the rulebook having willpower &gt; 7 is starting to get very strong and with willpower at 10, you're almost immune to many mind-altering effect. One freebee point for one willpower is quite cheap.<br /> But it doesn't really matter because WoD games are not about your character being strong and killing foes like in DnD. These games are about a (dark) story, about being a monster in a society blind to danger and about experiencing true horror. Even Mage, Hunters and Werewolves are, in their own way, monstrous.<br /> Players should not try to create the &quot;best&quot; character but one that'll shape the story in the way they want.<br /> Moreover being the &quot;perfect hero&quot;, the one without any weaknesses, is quite boring and should be discouraged as having a weakness is also adding opportunities for dramatic-effect.<br /> <br /> Finally player trying to have the perfect character based on the rulebook are forgetting one simple rule, the golden rule. They're experiencing a story and, if a ST is telling them they're being mind-controlled, so it is. The rulebook is just here to help the ST after all.<br /> So, in the end, the ST is free to set the difficulty of any dice roll as he judge fit and willpower is no more than a number.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":12400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","user":"GaryO","date":". 11-07-2016, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:36:04-08:00","id":999838,"title":"","content":"If all the PCs are at Willpower 10, so should the NPCs. Fair's fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:13:00-08:00","id":999855,"title":"","content":"I think WP gets a bit overrated depending a bit on the game line in question. WP is also very cheap with XP, so there's a lot of reasons to buy other things at character creation with your freebies because they are either XP expensive and/or opportunity cost expensive to get.<br /> <br /> As well, WP 10 doesn't really &quot;win&quot; anything. Not all mental powers use WP as difficulty (and many that do use temp. WP in the 20th books). Having access to 10 WP to spend it potent in any context, but it's a limited resource and every game has more cost effective options. It's usefulness is also highly variable based on your extant dice-pools and your opponents. A human with WP 10 isn't going to last long enough in a fight with a vampire with middling WP, Potence, and higher combat stats with the freebies they didn't use to get 10 WP instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:30:03-08:00","id":999880,"title":"","content":"I don't use Freebies.<br /> At chargen you receive 45 XP instead.<br /> This encourages a wide spread (because you get more dots on the low end than on the high end).<br /> And it discourages (over)specializing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:28:08-08:00","id":999949,"title":"","content":"I generally create the majority of my exceptional mortal NPCs with Willpower 7+ and my heroic mortal NPCs with Willpower 9+ (average mortals tend to be Willpower 3+ while competent mortals tend to be Willpower 5+). I tend to encourage by PCs to have Willpower 7+, regardless of type, to give them a chance of resisting mental powers, and I never let PCs into my game with a Willpower below 5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:19:05-08:00","id":999974,"title":"","content":"I'm not worried with the cost of WP in Freebies. Backgrounds are far more dangerous and cost the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:26:19-08:00","id":1000644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/999669-freebie-points-and-willpower?p=999974#post999974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not worried with the cost of WP in Freebies. Backgrounds are far more dangerous and cost the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but they are also more endangered because the majority of it is external to the PC.<br /> That doesn't mean you have to take them away, but the threat of losing it can hinder too overt usage of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:18:37-08:00","id":1001115,"title":"","content":"Not much different on WP. My first ST made it so hard to recover WP that we never had the chance of recovering enough to fill it in a year of game almost every three days or so. It was literally faster to buy Attribute dots. And all rolls of WP were made with temporary WP. We basically learned fast to not spend it unless at the direst of moments. I didn't sensed then that WP was worth the Freebies I spent on them, and it wasn't that much.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to talk a lot here about how much I find WoD broken as a system. But WP literally isn't worth more. Considering the other ways you can spend Freebies, just no. You can go for WP 10 if you want, without too much, but you can do a lot with the same cost, that you wouldn't be doing if you spend on WP.<br /> <br /> And there is absolutely no problem at all with maxing WP at character creation. You can max a lot of other traits as easily or even more. With 4 freebies and just maxing at normal distribution you can have 5 at both an Attribute and an Ability, and simply be the absolute apex of human accomplishment in that area. You can spend 14 Freebies and be at the apex of a Discipline, able, lets say, to take over the mind, spirit and body of a hapless victim to such extend that you can work on making her unable to even live without you afterwards. With 5 Freebies you can be so rich that no acquisition is above your financial prowess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T22:31:42-08:00","id":1001203,"title":"","content":"You need more imaginative players. I find that good players often spend little or no Freebies on Willpower, because they need them for little touches all over their sheet. Their character concept demands it. If you get unimaginative players, you can pretty much predict what they will buy: Strength 3, Dex 4, Stamina 3, all socials at 2, Perception 3, Int 2, Wits 3, Willpower 10. I've seen that sheet a thousand times when getting random people to play. It's the default spreed for unimaginative types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 11-10-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}